---
description: Avoid MSVC C2084 in UE unity builds.
globs: Source/**/*.h, Source/**/*.cpp
alwaysApply: true
---

# Unity build (C2084)

UE compiles the module as one file
(`Module.JoA_Arena.cpp`). Two `.cpp` files then
share one translation unit.

An anonymous-namespace function copied into a
second `.cpp` is defined twice. MSVC reports
C2084 (`already has a body`), then C2264 on
every call.

```cpp
// C2084. JoA_W_Play.cpp and JoA_W_Game.cpp
// both had this. Unity merged them.
namespace
{
	void DisableButtonFocus(UButton* Button)
	{
		Button->IsFocusable = false;
	}
}
```

Fix: one `inline` helper in a header both
files include. Here that is
`JoA_DisableButtonFocus` in
`UI/JoA_WidgetHelpers.h`.

Do not copy a free function, `static` helper,
or anonymous-namespace name into another
`.cpp` of this module. Share one definition,
or give that file its own name.
